This one's more serious than Heck-Hack.

When a character is confused or hallucinating, why shouldn't there be a 
small chance that the devotee will say the wrong thing or pray to the wrong 
god. This act would reduce piety, decrease luck or remove crowning. I 
suggest the possibility of removing crowning because it would have a 
beneficial effect of returning prayer timeout to normal. Most of the 
intrinsics granted by crowning are obtainable through mundane means. Once 
lost, one can't get it back.

The idea came to me while confused and hallucinating in a temple dedicated 
to Amaterasu Okami. My samurai was starving and a quick and effortless 
prayer sated his hunger. Hopefully no one will think this idea would 
needlessly increase the difficulty of Nethack.

